      "intro": "If your loved one is on a fixed income and struggling with high heating bills, Massachusetts Weatherization Assistance can provide free home improvements worth an average of $4,725. The program covers air sealing, insulation, heating system repairs, and weather-stripping at no cost to your loved one, and typically reduces heating bills by 25-35%.\n\nBecause this program coordinates with utility companies and uses trained contractors, your loved one gets professional-grade weatherization without the hassle of finding reliable workers or managing multiple estimates. Priority goes to households with elderly members, people with disabilities, or families with children under 6.\n\nThe catch: applications are only accepted October 1 through April 30 each year, and demand exceeds funding. Your loved one must qualify for the Low Income Home Energy Assistance Program (LIHEAP) income limits, generally 60% of state median income or 200% of federal poverty level.",
