      "intro": "If your loved one is 60+ and facing legal issues with Social Security, MassHealth, housing, or other civil matters, Massachusetts provides free legal advice through a dedicated senior helpline. The Massachusetts Senior Legal Helpline offers immediate phone consultations Monday through Friday 9am–12pm, helping seniors understand their rights and navigate legal problems.\n\nThe helpline covers the legal issues that affect seniors most: Social Security and SSI appeals, MassHealth eligibility disputes, housing problems including evictions and foreclosures, guardianship and power of attorney questions, veterans benefits, consumer protection, and nursing home issues. While most callers receive information and referrals rather than full attorney representation, the helpline can assess eligibility for free legal services and help complete applications during the call.",
      "savingsRange": "",
      "savingsSource": "Free service",
      "savingsVerified": false,
