        {
          "question": "Can my loved one get a free attorney through this helpline?",
          "answer": "Most callers receive information and referrals rather than free attorney representation. However, if your loved one qualifies for civil legal services (typically requiring low income below 125% of federal poverty level), the helpline staff can assess eligibility and help complete applications for free attorney programs during the call."
        },
        {
          "question": "What if my loved one has a criminal case or wants to sue for medical malpractice?",
          "answer": "The helpline only handles civil legal matters. They cannot help with criminal cases, medical malpractice, workers' compensation, or personal injury lawsuits (which are typically handled on a contingency basis by private attorneys)."
        },
        {
          "question": "What should I do if I can't get through during the limited hours?",
          "answer": "The helpline operates Monday-Friday 9am-12pm only. If you can't reach them, download the brochure from mass.gov for other legal resources, or contact your local Area Agency on Aging for additional referrals to legal services in your area."
        }
